  "title": "Time, days & months",
  "goal": "Tell the time, name the days and months, and talk about today, yesterday and tomorrow.",
  "intro": "Kannada days of the week are named after the planets, like their Sanskrit and European counterparts: ಸೋಮ (Moon) → Monday, ಶನಿ (Saturn) → Saturday. For months, everyday life uses the **English names** (ಜನವರಿ, ಫೆಬ್ರವರಿ ...), while festivals follow the traditional lunar calendar starting with ಚೈತ್ರ at ಯುಗಾದಿ, the Kannada New Year in March/April.\n\nTelling time uses ಗಂಟೆ 'hour, o'clock' (literally 'bell') and the dative -ಗೆ for 'at'.",
